What is the difference between static and instance variables?


1. Static Variable
Static variable poori class ka hota hai. Iski sirf ek shared copy hoti hai, jise class ke saare objects use kar sakte hain.

Example: Classroom ki ek wall clock, jise saare bachche dekhte hain.
static String classroom = "Sunshine";


Agar static variable ki value change karte hain, toh us class ke sabhi objects ko updated value dikhegi.

2. Instance Variable
Instance variable har object ka apna hota hai. Har object ke paas iski alag copy hoti hai.

Example: Har bachche ka apna teddy bear. Ek bachche ka teddy change karne se doosre bachche ka teddy nahi badlega.
String toy = "Teddy";


Agar ek object ke instance variable ki value change karte hain, toh doosre objects ki values par koi asar nahi padta.
Example
class Child {
    static String classroom = "Sunshine";
    String toy;
}


- classroom → Static variable, sabhi objects ke liye shared.
- toy → Instance variable, har object ke liye alag.
Interview mein yaad rakhne wali line:
- Static = Sabka ek (shared copy).
- Instance = Har object ka apna (separate copy).


