Q9. Can main() method be overloaded in Java?
Yes, you can overload main() like any other method. However, the JVM will only call the standard public static void main(String[] args) as the entry point.
The overloaded versions can be called explicitly within the code.


Summary: Java mein main() method ko overload kar sakte hain, jaise main(int val) ya main(String args). Lekin JVM program start karne ke liye sirf standard public static void main(String[] args) method ko call karta hai. Baaki overloaded main() methods ko humein code ke andar se manually call karna padta hai.
